{"name":"Male Betta","hex":"#347699","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"male","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging to the sex which typically produces sperm, or to the gender which is typically associated with it. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Characteristic of this sex/gender."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the male (masculine) sex or gender.\nA human member of the masculine sex or gender.\n\nAn animal of the sex that has testes.\nA plant of the masculine sex.","A human member of the masculine sex or gender."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male"},{"term":"betta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any fish of the genus Betta, especially Betta splendens (the Siamese fighting fish)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pronunciation spelling of better, comparative of good."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/betta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Male","blocks":[{"text":"Male is the sex of an organism that produces, or is organized to produce, the gamete known as sperm, which fuses with the larger female gamete, or ovum, in the process of fertilisation. A male organism cannot reproduce sexually without access to at least one ovum from a female, but some organisms can reproduce both sexually and asexually. Most male mammals, including male humans, have a Y chromosome, which codes for the production of larger amounts of testosterone to develop male reproductive organs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Male_symbol_%28bold%2C_color%29.svg/330px-Male_symbol_%28bold%2C_color%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Male","wikidata":"Q44148"},{"title":"Betta","blocks":[{"text":"Betta is a large genus of small, active, often colorful, freshwater ray-finned fishes, in the gourami family (Osphronemidae). The best known Betta species is B. splendens, commonly known as the Siamese fighting fish and often kept as an aquarium pet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Betta_albimarginata_060311_8.jpg/330px-Betta_albimarginata_060311_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betta","wikidata":"Q4164940"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Anterior_view_of_human_female_and_male%2C_with_labels_2.png/500px-Anterior_view_of_human_female_and_male%2C_with_labels_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Anterior_view_of_human_female_and_male%2C_with_labels_2.png/500px-Anterior_view_of_human_female_and_male%2C_with_labels_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of an adult male human, with an adult female for comparison. Both models have partially shaved body hair; e.g. clean-shaven pubic regions.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnterior_view_of_human_female_and_male%2C_with_labels_2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg/500px-Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg/1280px-Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg/500px-Kampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Betta splendens, the Siamese fighting fish, is often referred to simply as a \"betta\" in the U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKampffisch_betta_splendenscele4.jpg"},{"srcset":"htt